module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.IntegralApproximation.Subalgebra
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraAffineSections.Basic

/-!
# The finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of an integral algebra sheaf

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras.  [Stacks, Tag 0817] presents
an *integral* quasi-coherent `A` as the directed colimit of its **finite** quasi-coherent
subalgebras.  [Stacks, Tag 05JT] presents a quasi-coherent `A` as the directed colimit of its
**finite type** quasi-coherent subalgebras.  When `A` is integral the two indexing categories are
the same, because a finite type subalgebra of an integral algebra sheaf is finite
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IntegralSubalgebras.isFiniteType_iff_isFinite_of_mono`), and tag 0817
is tag 05JT transported along that identification.

This file supplies the missing vocabulary — the category of finite quasi-coherent subalgebras,
its diagram and its canonical cocone — and performs the transport.  No new mathematics: the
identification of the two predicates and both assertions of tag 05JT that are available are
proved elsewhere in the library with complete proofs; what is new is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras.FiniteSubalgebra` and its transport.

## Main definitions

* `FiniteSubalgebra A`: the full subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Subobject A` on the subobjects
  that are quasi-coherent and finite.
* `finiteSubalgebraDiagram A` and `finiteSubalgebraCocone A`: that category viewed as a diagram
  of algebra sheaves, and its canonical cocone with vertex `A` and the inclusions as components.
* `equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra`: for integral `A`, the equivalence with the category
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A` of tag 05JT.  It is the
  identity on objects and on morphisms; only the *property* carried by an object changes.

## Main results

* `isFiltered_finiteSubalgebra`: **the directedness assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0817]**, with no
  hypothesis on `X` whatsoever — not quasi-compactness, not quasi-separatedness, not affineness.
  It is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`, which
  is itself unconditional, transported along `equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra`.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`: **the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0817]**,
  for a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, from the tag 05JT form of the same statement in
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`, along the same equivalence.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_isAffine`: the special case of an affine scheme,
  which predates the general one and goes through a different sections statement.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections`: the colimit assertion from the
  affine sections statement alone, for any scheme.  This is the form in which the transport is
  genuinely hypothesis-free; everything missing is inside `hsec`.
* `exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff` and `exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine`: the
  affine sections statement in tag 0817's own vocabulary — a section comes from a finite
  quasi-coherent subalgebra exactly when it comes from a finite type one.

## The covering set of the tag

Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0817] covers *two* assertions, directedness and the colimit, so its
covering set is the two declarations `isFiltered_finiteSubalgebra` and
`nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`, and the attribute sits on both.  The tag's third
assertion is part (2), carried by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag0817PartTwo.exists_small_index_finite_finitePresentation`.

Part (2) of the tag — an integral algebra sheaf as a colimit of algebra sheaves that are finite
*and of finite presentation* — is a separate assertion and is not proved here.  It **is** proved,
as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag0817PartTwo.exists_small_index_finite_finitePresentation`, which
carries the tag for that third assertion: part (1) at a `u`-small index together with
[Stacks, Tag 086N] at a `u`-small index, spliced by
`Stacks.FinitelyPresentableComposition.exists_directed_index_algebraSheaf`, whose presentability
hypothesis holds along those cocones by [Stacks, Tag 01ZC] carried across the relative-spectrum
anti-equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 01SA].  The splice does **not** need [Stacks, Tag 01BS] for
algebra sheaves, which remains absent.

The proposition that used to be the one input this file waited on — for `X` quasi-compact and
quasi-separated, `A` quasi-coherent, `V` an affine open and `x` a section of `A` over `V`, a
finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A` **on the whole of `X`** having `x` among its
sections over `V` — is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section`, where
the subalgebra is the one generated by a finite type quasi-coherent submodule supplied by
[Stacks, Tag 01PF].

## Implementation notes

The transport is an equivalence rather than a rewrite of the defining predicate.  `IsFiltered`
and `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit` both have transport lemmas along an equivalence
(`CategoryTheory.IsFiltered.of_equivalence` and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit.whiskerEquivalence`), whereas rewriting the predicate inside
`IsFiltered (ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory _)` has to move the `Category` instance too.

`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.ιOfLE` is the identity on underlying subobjects, so
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.ιOfLECompιIso` is `CategoryTheory.Iso.refl`; that is why the unit
and counit of `equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra` are componentwise `Iso.refl`, and why the whiskered
cocone of tag 05JT is `finiteSubalgebraCocone A` definitionally.

Both directions of the equivalence need integrality, in opposite ways: finite implies finite type
for any algebra sheaf (`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFinite.isFiniteType`), while finite
type implies finite only over an integral `A`, which is [Stacks, Tag 02JJ] on affine sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.RelativeSpec

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The property of a subobject of an algebra sheaf of being quasi-coherent and finite.  This is
the property cutting out the indexing category of [Stacks, Tag 0817]. -/
abbrev isQuasicoherentAndFinite (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : ObjectProperty (Subobject A) :=
  fun B => (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsFinite

/-- The property of a subobject of an algebra sheaf of being quasi-coherent and of finite type.
This is the property cutting out the indexing category of [Stacks, Tag 05JT], and it is the
defining property of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra`. -/
abbrev isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : ObjectProperty (Subobject A) :=
  fun B => (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsFiniteType

/-- **The category of finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of an algebra sheaf.**  This is the full
subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Subobject A` on the subobjects whose underlying algebra sheaf is
quasi-coherent and finite.  It is the indexing category of [Stacks, Tag 0817]. -/
abbrev FiniteSubalgebra (A : AlgebraSheaf X) :=
  (isQuasicoherentAndFinite A).FullSubcategory

/-- The diagram consisting of all finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A`. -/
def finiteSubalgebraDiagram (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : FiniteSubalgebra A ⥤ AlgebraSheaf X :=
  ObjectProperty.ι _ ⋙ Subobject.underlying

/-- The canonical cocone of all finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A`, with vertex `A` and
with the inclusions of the subobjects as its components. -/
def finiteSubalgebraCocone (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : Cocone (finiteSubalgebraDiagram A) :=
  Cocone.mk A
    { app := fun B => B.obj.arrow
      naturality := fun _ _ f => Subobject.underlying_arrow f.hom }

/-- The diagram `finiteSubalgebraDiagram A` sends a finite subalgebra to its underlying algebra
sheaf. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteSubalgebraDiagram_obj (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) :
    (finiteSubalgebraDiagram A).obj B = (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X) :=
  rfl

/-- The vertex of `finiteSubalgebraCocone A` is `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteSubalgebraCocone_pt (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : (finiteSubalgebraCocone A).pt = A :=
  rfl

/-- The component of `finiteSubalgebraCocone A` at a finite subalgebra `B` is the inclusion of `B`
into `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteSubalgebraCocone_ι_app (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) :
    (finiteSubalgebraCocone A).ι.app B = B.obj.arrow :=
  rfl

/-- A quasi-coherent finite subobject of an algebra sheaf is quasi-coherent of finite type.  This
direction needs no hypothesis on the ambient algebra sheaf. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentAndFinite_le (A : AlgebraSheaf X) :
    isQuasicoherentAndFinite A ≤ isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType A :=
  fun _ hB => ⟨hB.1, hB.2.isFiniteType⟩

/-- A quasi-coherent finite type subobject of an **integral** algebra sheaf is finite.  This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IntegralSubalgebras.isFinite_subobject`, i.e. [Stacks, Tag 02JJ] on the
sections over the affine opens. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType_le {A : AlgebraSheaf X} (hA : A.IsIntegral) :
    isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType A ≤ isQuasicoherentAndFinite A :=
  fun B hB => ⟨hB.1, IntegralSubalgebras.isFinite_subobject hA B hB.2⟩

/-- **For an integral algebra sheaf the indexing categories of tags 0817 and 05JT agree.**  The
equivalence is the identity on underlying subobjects and on morphisms; only the property recorded
by an object differs, and the two properties are equivalent by [Stacks, Tag 02JJ]. -/
def equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra {A : AlgebraSheaf X} (hA : A.IsIntegral) :
    FiniteSubalgebra A ≌ FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A where
  functor := ObjectProperty.ιOfLE (isQuasicoherentAndFinite_le A)
  inverse := ObjectProperty.ιOfLE (isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType_le hA)
  unitIso := NatIso.ofComponents fun _ => Iso.refl _
  counitIso := NatIso.ofComponents fun _ => Iso.refl _

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0817], the directedness assertion.**  The finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of
an integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras form a filtered category.

No hypothesis on `X` is used: not quasi-compactness, not quasi-separatedness, not Noetherian and
not affineness.  This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`,
which is unconditional, transported along `equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra`.

This is one of the two declarations covering part (1) of the tag; the other is
`nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`. -/
@[stacks 0817 "part (1), the directedness assertion: the finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of an
integral quasi-coherent algebra sheaf form a filtered category; no hypothesis on X"]
theorem isFiltered_finiteSubalgebra (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (hAqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A)
    (hAint : A.IsIntegral) : IsFiltered (FiniteSubalgebra A) :=
  have := FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra A hAqc
  IsFiltered.of_equivalence (equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra hAint).symm

/-- **For an integral algebra sheaf, coming from a finite subalgebra and coming from a finite
type subalgebra are the same condition on a section.**  Both directions are the object-level
inclusions of `equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra`, which leave the subobject and its inclusion morphism
untouched; this is what lets the affine sections statement of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] be read as the
affine sections statement of [Stacks, Tag 0817]. -/
theorem exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff {A : AlgebraSheaf X} (hAint : A.IsIntegral)
    {U : X.Opens} (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    (∃ (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x) ↔
      ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
        (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
          B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨B, y, hy⟩
    exact ⟨⟨B.obj, isQuasicoherentAndFinite_le A B.obj B.property⟩, y, hy⟩
  · rintro ⟨B, y, hy⟩
    exact ⟨⟨B.obj, isQuasicoherentAndFiniteType_le hAint B.obj B.property⟩, y, hy⟩

/-- **The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0817] from the affine sections statement alone.**  An
integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras is the colimit of its finite
quasi-coherent subalgebras, with the canonical inclusions, as soon as every section over every
affine open comes from one of them.

No hypothesis on `X` is used.  This is the form in which the transport along
`equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra` costs nothing: everything tag 0817 still owes is inside `hsec`. -/
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hAqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) (hAint : A.IsIntegral)
    (hsec : ∀ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → ∀ x : A.right.obj.obj (op U),
      ∃ (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteSubalgebraCocone A)) := by
  obtain ⟨hc⟩ := FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections A hAqc
    fun U hU x => (exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff hAint x).mp (hsec U hU x)
  exact ⟨hc.whiskerEquivalence (equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra hAint)⟩

/-- **The affine sections statement of [Stacks, Tag 0817] on an affine scheme.**  On an affine
scheme, every section of an integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras over
every affine open comes from a finite quasi-coherent subalgebra.

This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraAffineSections.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine`
read through `exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff`. -/
theorem exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine [IsAffine X] (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hAqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) (hAint : A.IsIntegral) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
      B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x :=
  (exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff hAint x).mpr
    (SubalgebraAffineSections.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine A hAqc hU x)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0817, the colimit assertion of part (1).**  On a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated scheme an integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras is the
colimit of the canonical diagram of all its finite quasi-coherent subalgebras, with the
inclusions of the subobjects as the structure morphisms.

For an integral algebra sheaf a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra is finite
([Stacks, Tag 02JJ] on affine sections), so this is the tag 05JT form of the same statement,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`'s
`nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone`, transported along
`equivFiniteTypeSubalgebra`. -/
@[stacks 0817 "part (1), the colimit assertion: an integral quasi-coherent algebra sheaf is the
colimit of its finite quasi-coherent subalgebras, for X quasi-compact and quasi-separated"]
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (hAqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) (hAint : A.IsIntegral) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections A hAqc hAint fun U hU x =>
    (exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_iff hAint x).mpr
      (SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section A hAqc U hU x)

/-- **The colimit assertion of part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0817] for an affine scheme.**  An
integral quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras on an affine scheme is the colimit of
its finite quasi-coherent subalgebras, with the canonical inclusions.

This is a special case of `nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`, which it predates; it is
kept because it goes through a different sections statement, the affine-scheme one of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraAffineSections`, which needs no [Stacks, Tag 01PF]. -/
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_isAffine [IsAffine X] (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hAqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) (hAint : A.IsIntegral) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections A hAqc hAint
    fun _ hU x => exists_finiteSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine A hAqc hAint hU x

/-- Every object of the diagram of [Stacks, Tag 0817] is a quasi-coherent, finite algebra sheaf.
Compared with the conclusion of tag 0817 the missing condition is finite presentation, which is
what [Stacks, Tag 086N] supplies. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_and_isFinite_finiteSubalgebraDiagram_obj (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (B : FiniteSubalgebra A) :
    ((finiteSubalgebraDiagram A).obj B).IsQuasicoherent ∧
      ((finiteSubalgebraDiagram A).obj B).IsFinite :=
  B.property

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras

end


